---
description: Comment discipline — no narrative, history, or what-comments
alwaysApply: true
---

A comment may state only a current constraint or behaviour the code cannot
show — written for the next reader, not the reviewer.

Do not write:
- "what" comments that narrate the next line
- history: "used to…", "fixes the bug where…", "not a no-op"
- rationale or design justification
- docstrings that restate the signature

Before writing a comment, try to make it unnecessary: a named constant, a better
name, a smaller unit. Match the comment density of the surrounding file; when in
doubt, omit it.

Rationale belongs in the commit message or `AGENTS.md`, not in the code.
